---
import StartPage from '@learn/shared/components/StartPage.astro';
import { withBase } from '@learn/shared/lib/content.ts';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<StartPage site={site}>
  <p>
    <strong>Every PART of <code>L1-coding-html-css.md</code> is one lesson</strong> at
    <a href={withBase('/learn/')}>/learn/</a>. Inside a lesson, each top-level bullet of the source is its own
    section, in the same order, with an explanation, a code snippet where code helps, and a live demo,
    playground or “Try it” exercise with a model answer. The Part's intuition anchors, mastery checks
    (with model answers), build project and taste note follow at the end.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The training file <code>T1-coding-html-css.md</code> is the <a href={withBase('/dojo/')}>dojo</a></strong>:
    drill tables get timers, belt gates record passes, lists become checklists, prediction sets track your
    hit-rate, and the logbook exports <code>LOG.md</code>. Capstones, the learning path and the resource
    library each have their own page, and the <a href={withBase('/coverage/')}>coverage matrix</a> proves nothing was skipped.
  </p>
  <p>
    Progress (completed parts, ticks, drill times) is stored only in this browser. Nothing is sent anywhere.
  </p>
</StartPage>
